1. WHO CAN USE THE COMMUNITY LICENCE

You may use the Software under the Community Licence if at least one of these
applies to you:

  a. Small organisations. You are an individual, or an organisation, whose
     annual gross revenue was less than US$1,000,000 (or its equivalent in
     another currency) in its most recent financial year. An organisation
     counts the revenue of all its affiliates as well as its own.

  b. Non-profits and education. You are a registered charity or other
     not-for-profit organisation, or an accredited school, college or
     university, using the Software for its not-for-profit or educational
     work.

  c. Open source. You use the Software in a project that is published, with
     its full source code, under a licence approved by the Open Source
     Initiative. This condition covers your use of the Software in that
     project only.

  d. Evaluation and development. You use the Software only to evaluate it, or
     to develop and test your own software, and not in production.

  e. Indirect use. You use the Software only because a product made by someone
     else includes it or depends on it, and you don't use the Software or its
     programming interfaces directly.

"Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with an organisation. "Control" means owning more than 50% of
the voting shares or other ownership interest, or having the power to direct
the entity's management.

"Production" means any use of the Software other than evaluating it, or
developing and testing software with it. It includes:

  - running the Software, or software that includes it, in your own
    operations;
  - distributing the Software, or software that includes it, to others,
    whether for payment or free of charge; and
  - providing a service to others that uses the Software.

If you stop meeting the conditions you relied on, for example because your
revenue reaches the limit in 1a, you have 90 days to get a Commercial Licence.
After that, your rights under the Community Licence end.


